# 2026-07-13 00:49:21.138668
+Implement an async method `extractCleanText(url: string): Promise<string>` inside browser_manager.ts using our Playwright setup. It must initialize headless Chromium, navigate to the url waiting for networkidle, strip out inline <script> and <style> tags from the body, extract clean innerText, and handle errors safely by closing the page.

# 2026-07-13 01:00:18.964497
+n

# 2026-07-13 01:05:37.811688
+/add packages/browser/browser_manager.ts

# 2026-07-13 01:06:06.054296
+The target file matches failed because you are trying to guess middle blocks. Please look at the very last closing curly brace '}' of the BrowserManager class at the bottom of packages/browser/browser_manager.ts. 
+
+Create a SEARCH/REPLACE block that replaces that final brace to insert this method right before it:
+
+  async extractCleanText(url: string): Promise<string> {
+    const context = await this.browser.newContext();
+    const page = await context.newPage();
+    try {
+      await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });
+      await page.evaluate(() => {
+        const elements = document.querySelectorAll('script, style');
+        elements.forEach(el => el.remove());
+      });
+      const cleanText = await page.evaluate(() => document.body.innerText);
+      return cleanText;
+    } catch (error) {
+      console.error(`Failed text extraction for ${url}:`, error);
+      throw error;
+    } finally {
+      await page.close();
+      await context.close();
+    }
+  }

